  "steps": [
    "<strong>Prepare Tofu:</strong> Bring a saucepan of water to the boil with MSG and salt. Add tofu and simmer 7–8 min. Drain and allow to steam-dry in a colander until surface moisture evaporates.",
    "Preheat oven to 200°C. Toss tofu with soy sauce, olive oil, and cornstarch. Spread on a lined tray and bake 20–25 min, turning halfway, until golden and crisp.",
    "<strong>Cook Noodles:</strong> Boil udon noodles in salted water 4–5 min until al dente. Drain and rinse under cold water; set aside.",
    "<strong>Make Sauce:</strong> Whisk tahini, soy sauce, maple syrup, rice vinegar, chilli oil, and water until smooth and pourable.",
    "Heat olive oil in a large pan over medium-high. Stir-fry ginger and garlic ~1 min until fragrant. Add broccoli and kale; cook ~4 min until just tender.",
    "Add noodles, baked tofu, sauce, and spring onions. Toss well to coat and heat through.",
    "Serve topped with mixed sesame seeds. Finish with extra soy sauce or a squeeze of lime if desired."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Simmering tofu first gives it a firmer, meatier texture.",
    "Swap udon for rice noodles or soba if preferred.",
    "Add extra chilli oil or crispy chilli for more heat."
  ]
